cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use widethink or the Hidden Requirements benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "widethink: brain-inspired wide thinking for LLMs"
abstract: >-
  A harness between the user and a language model that decides what the model
  thinks about at each step, using the mechanisms of a digital brain's thought
  stream (lottery selection, satiation, inhibition of return, fading, value pull,
  capture by surprise, and branches cued by the user's context), together with a
  benchmark of tasks whose standard solution does not fit the user's context.
authors:
  - given-names: Egor
    alias: egor-gamedev
repository-code: "https://github.com/egor-gamedev/widethink"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0.dev0
keywords:
  - large language models
  - reasoning
  - test-time compute
  - tree of thoughts
  - benchmark
  - hidden requirements
